# Normalise every text file to LF, both in the repo and in the working tree.
# Added 19 Jul 2026 after a whole-tree CRLF flip produced a ~12,700-line phantom diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — git must never touch their bytes.
*.avif binary
*.webp binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary

# data/health-log.jsonl is an APPEND-ONLY event log (ROADMAP recording policy, layer 2): one JSON
# object per line, one line per system-health run, read by scripts and never by hand.
#
# `merge=union` tells git to keep BOTH sides' lines instead of raising a conflict. That is the
# correct resolution for this file and the only one ever wanted - it is what was applied by hand
# three separate times on 28-29 Jul 2026 (two merges and one stash-pop).
#
# It is here for a sharper reason than convenience. When this file DOES conflict, git writes
# <<<<<<< / ======= / >>>>>>> markers into it, and those lines are not valid JSON. A conflicted
# health log is a log that every consuming script chokes on, and on 29 Jul one sat unnoticed in the
# working tree with three invalid lines in it. Union removes that failure mode entirely.
#
# Union can leave records slightly out of timestamp order, and can keep a duplicate. Both are
# harmless here and deliberately preferred: scripts/health-log-dedupe.mjs says it plainly - "losing
# history is much worse than keeping a duplicate".
#
# NOTE this does not stop `git switch` refusing while the file is dirty - merge drivers apply to
# merges, not checkouts. `system-health` appends on every run, so if a branch switch aborts, commit
# or `git checkout -- data/health-log.jsonl` first. The line is regenerated on the next run.
data/health-log.jsonl merge=union
